WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:05.830
- It's December the 17th, 2020,

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.020
and I never thought that I would be here

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.033
at this place at this time in my life.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.900
It was kind of rough
there for a moment, well,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.480
longer than a moment.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:17.430
And I'd like to start off this,

00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:20.632
(sighs)

00:00:20.632 --> 00:00:25.223
this topic as something that
happened to me last night.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:30.770
I got up for work last night
and I paid my mom a visit

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.870
because it's been about three
months since I last seen her

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.160
but I talk to her almost every day.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:41.160
And while I was in there,
and when I first got there,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.540
I couldn't even hug her, man.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.770
Because of her age, her condition,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.590
the things she's going
through, she's working with.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:51.113
She's got some health issues as she's 74,

00:00:54.055 --> 00:00:55.173
I think 76 years old.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.930
And I wanted to greet her
with a kiss on the forehead,

00:01:00.930 --> 00:01:03.200
here, here, here, and on the lips

00:01:04.047 --> 00:01:04.880
'cause that's how I greeted her

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:06.763
when I first came home from prison.

00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:12.430
And I got that concept
from a book I was reading

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.243
and the book was,

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:21.530
the writer of the book said
her son had a best friend

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:24.530
whose father was an
alcoholic who lost his mom

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:26.370
when he was four years old

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.360
and his father was mean to him

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.420
and she knew his father
was mistreating him.

00:01:31.420 --> 00:01:34.420
Not in the ways of physical
abuse but verbally.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:37.420
He wasn't there for him
because he was always drunk.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.100
So every time her son
would bring his best friend

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.100
over to the house,

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.940
she would greet him with
a kiss on the forehead,

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:46.410
the two left side cheeks and on the lips

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.230
and said, "I love you."

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.590
And when I read that,

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.873
I cried and I experienced that in prison.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:01:56.620
That was like two and a
half years before parole.

00:01:56.620 --> 00:01:59.160
I read that paragraph in that book

00:02:00.261 --> 00:02:01.370
and two and a half years later,

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.733
when I was released from
motherfucking prison,

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:08.780
first place I went to was my mom's place.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.470
I kissed her on the
forehead, both her cheeks,

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:12.303
and on her lips,

00:02:12.303 --> 00:02:13.290
and I said, "I love you."

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.747
She said, "You never did that before.

00:02:17.747 --> 00:02:19.210
"Where'd this come from?"

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.597
I said, "From a book that I read."

00:02:23.266 --> 00:02:24.790
And it had meant something to me

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:26.490
and now it means something to her.

00:02:27.505 --> 00:02:30.210
And it all came back full
circle last night when I went

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.630
to her house and I couldn't
greet her in that way

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.463
to show her.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.676
Her birthday was September
and I had missed it

00:02:39.676 --> 00:02:41.360
because I didn't have the money.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.780
So what happened was when I
got to her place last night,

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.727
I said, "Look mom, I
have to run to the store

00:02:45.727 --> 00:02:48.760
"to get a few things. I'll be right back."

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.523
I went to the Ralph's Supermarket.

00:02:52.631 --> 00:02:55.403
It took me about 45 minutes
to find the right card,

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.967
but I found it and I presented it to her.

00:03:02.896 --> 00:03:03.729
And she read it.

00:03:08.177 --> 00:03:09.470
She said, "Put your mask on."

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.683
I put my mask on.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.310
She just hugged me and held me.

00:03:20.983 --> 00:03:23.050
(sighs)

00:03:23.050 --> 00:03:25.423
And that's how I left her house, man,

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.590
and said, "I love you."

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.152
And words can't describe what
it feels like just to get

00:03:31.152 --> 00:03:32.453
that feeling.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.470
'Cause today, I'm not
on time for birthdays

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:40.730
and Christmases and
holidays and shit like that.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.200
Sometimes, they're on, but
it's like hit and miss with me

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.310
'cause I have two left feet.

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:48.158
I'm like the little train that could.

00:03:48.158 --> 00:03:51.020
I want to think I have,
a new life is good,

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.690
and I got my shit together,

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.150
but in all honesty, I don't, man.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.520
It's trial and error.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.340
Even dealing with my
family is hit and miss

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.430
because all of the times
that I was in prison,

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.300
all of the time, all the rehabs,

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.020
all of the trips, the bullshit,

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.460
just had me further and further away

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.390
from dealing with my loved ones.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.230
Crack, everything,

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:14.630
I gave crack everything that I had.

00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.130
My mind, my body, damn and my soul.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:19.280
Family?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.280
Shit, put them in a pipe and smoke them.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:24.443
Relationships, I don't give a fuck.

00:04:25.802 --> 00:04:28.013
Jobs? Man, that's shit.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.773
You can't pay me to work.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.373
Are you serious?

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:39.630
And last night just showed
me that there's a lot

00:04:40.010 --> 00:04:41.253
of work ahead for me.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:44.250
There's a lot of work ahead for me, man.

00:04:45.402 --> 00:04:47.610
And I'd like to start off with, hey,

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:50.730
shit, man, I've been working
now for about three months

00:04:50.730 --> 00:04:53.840
and I work in the construction field,

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:56.733
but my thing is under the table.

00:04:56.733 --> 00:04:59.100
And why under the table?

00:04:59.100 --> 00:05:01.693
Because that's the way
it turned out for me.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:07.230
I was in jail, man, for about,

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.200
how long have I been home?

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.800
I've been home from
prison (counts silently)

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:16.122
May of 2017 and I was in the gym every day

00:05:16.122 --> 00:05:20.650
from May 2017 up until
about eight months ago

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:26.053
before the COVID hit, COVID-19,
and they shut it down.

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.890
And the first time they shut it down, man,

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.590
I was depressed for about seven days.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:36.590
I had withdrawals like I had
flu symptoms and I didn't eat,

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.720
I didn't sleep, I didn't drink water,

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.370
nothing for about four days.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.270
Then three days after
that, still depressed.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.970
It took me about a week and a half

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.380
to get through it.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.130
And then they opened back up the gyms

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:55.580
and I was like hip, hip, hurray.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.110
And I went for the next two weeks

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.773
and they shut it down again.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:06.740
And I remember being in my room

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:11.653
and I was in bed and I was
just thinking to myself,

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.813
if something doesn't happen,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.500
then mind, body, and spirit,

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.080
I just saw myself sinking in quicksand.

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:24.440
I just saw myself just sinking and sinking

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.040
without nobody being able to help,

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:29.450
to lend a hand down to get me up out that.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.030
And that's what it felt like, man.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:35.150
I said I can't go through what
I went through the first time

00:06:35.150 --> 00:06:38.780
they shut it down, not eating, sleeping,

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:40.370
and being depressed, man.

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.003
It fucked me up.

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:45.153
Why?

00:06:45.153 --> 00:06:47.040
The gym is my foundation.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.010
I've been dealing with the
gym now for the past 30 years.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.870
The gym helped me through my 20s,

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:52.847
it helped me through my 30s,

00:06:52.847 --> 00:06:55.030
and it helped me through my 40s.

00:06:55.030 --> 00:07:00.030
That's all I had, was my body,
my looks to get me through.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:04.280
And it worked far as
relationships with women.

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:06.360
Women were attracted to the body,

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:10.573
the size, the look, and
that's what carried me, man.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:15.270
It didn't help me stay out of prison,

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.630
it didn't help me stay out
of motherfucking rehabs,

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:20.000
it didn't help me keep from being homeless

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.730
over and over and over again.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.403
But it worked with the
women, with the ladies.

00:07:26.770 --> 00:07:28.820
And it only worked for so long

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:30.930
because as soon as the crack
start knocking on the door,

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:31.973
there I go.

00:07:34.540 --> 00:07:37.160
And eventually, I put her in
a pipe and smoked her up too,

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.380
with the furniture, and
everything else that come with it,

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.280
the house, the car, all that bullshit.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.040
'Cause after I take a hit,

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.380
everything is a crack coupon, man.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:47.460
It's just a coupon.

00:07:47.460 --> 00:07:49.030
Matter of time,

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.730
going out of business sale.

00:07:51.997 --> 00:07:53.547
And that's just the way it was.

00:07:55.230 --> 00:08:00.230
And so I'm in my room and
I'm thinking to myself,

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.310
I can't go through what I
went through the first time.

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:07.760
And creator, you have to
show me something, please.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:08.840
That next day,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:11.520
I got a phone call from
an old friend of mine.

00:08:11.520 --> 00:08:13.450
He said, "Hey, would you like to work?"

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.420
And this happened to be the weekend.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:16.960
I said, "Sure."

00:08:16.960 --> 00:08:18.580
He came to my house and got me

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:21.310
and I've been working ever since.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:22.743
It's going on four months.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.580
I learned how to paint,

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:27.840
I learned how to lay cement,

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:31.360
and now I'm refurbishing
floors, wood floors.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:35.210
And I work seven days a week

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:37.310
or six days a week now,

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.210
hit and miss, it all depends.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:41.220
Now truth be told,

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:43.930
I'm not getting paid what
I'm supposed to be paid

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.210
because like I said,

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:48.530
I'm not certified, qualified,
and none of that shit,

00:08:48.530 --> 00:08:52.100
but where I get paid is in the experience,

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:55.023
being taught something that
I've never been taught before.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:58.843
Everything I'm learning in my 50s,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.260
I should've had that shit
in my 20s, 30s, and 40s,

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.340
but see how I had to twist it?

00:09:05.340 --> 00:09:07.223
I had the gym in my 20s, 30s, and 40s

00:09:07.223 --> 00:09:10.100
and the only thing that
worked was the outside.

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:11.530
So it didn't give me that feeling

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:13.740
that I needed on the inside.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:17.020
Because what I got from the
inside was everybody's approval,

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:19.160
everybody's accolades or the double-takes

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.250
and all that bullshit when
I'm walking down the street.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:23.070
Oh, big man, hey, this, that.

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:23.903
That's what kept me going,

00:09:23.903 --> 00:09:25.220
that's what kept me motivated,

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:27.210
that's what kept my ass in the gym,

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.080
everybody else's approval,

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.283
how they looked at me.

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:38.240
Flip side of the coin is when
I do a good job on the floor

00:09:38.500 --> 00:09:40.557
and I see my work and my
boss come behind me say,

00:09:40.557 --> 00:09:42.053
"Hey, man, that's a good job.

00:09:43.507 --> 00:09:44.597
"You did good today, man.

00:09:44.597 --> 00:09:45.760
"I'm proud of you."

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:47.820
Soon as I get my
motherfucking ass back home,

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.483
I cry like a baby.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:53.750
I cry.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:54.583
You know why?

00:09:54.583 --> 00:09:56.880
'Cause every time I think about it,

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.060
it takes me back to when
I was 14, 15, 16 years old

00:10:03.143 --> 00:10:04.620
and all the, (sighs)

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.226
and where I was at, at
that time of my life.

00:10:07.226 --> 00:10:10.860
So emotionally, I feel,

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:14.300
I get that feeling of
being 15 years old or 16

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.330
when my boss say, "Hey,
man, you did a good job."

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:20.327
Or when something, when a light
goes on my mind and I say,

00:10:20.327 --> 00:10:22.473
"Oh, I got it."

00:10:22.473 --> 00:10:23.390
Then the feeling comes up

00:10:23.390 --> 00:10:25.500
but not as a 53 years old

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:27.723
but as a 15-year-old emotionally.

00:10:29.024 --> 00:10:30.600
That shit is crazy.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:32.560
I still don't understand it.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.023
I still don't get it.

00:10:35.872 --> 00:10:36.820
There's a lot I don't get.

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:38.700
There's a lot that I missed

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.513
but it's okay.

00:10:41.513 --> 00:10:42.346
It's okay.

00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.690
Shit, there's some
questions that I might have

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:48.050
that I might never get an answer to,

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:49.200
but I'm okay with that.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:51.800
I'm cool with that, shit.

00:10:54.761 --> 00:10:56.761
(sighs)

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:02.550
Aside from working,

00:11:07.481 --> 00:11:08.710
(sighs)

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:12.430
I'm just at a place, man,
where I'm learning how

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:16.840
to deal with me, be good
to me, treat myself,

00:11:16.840 --> 00:11:20.370
take care of me, and everything
else that comes with it.

00:11:20.370 --> 00:11:25.370
It's not easy me being on
my own, in my own place,

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:28.990
being responsible for me,
taking responsibility,

00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:31.130
and all that because aside from me,

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:33.440
there's other people
that I have to deal with

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.553
and interact with.

00:11:35.526 --> 00:11:38.850
And that bridge, man, that's a long bridge

00:11:38.850 --> 00:11:40.490
that I have to cross, man.

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:42.903
Just to be like that
with my immediate family.

00:11:44.560 --> 00:11:47.310
My brother's starting to come
around slowly but surely.

00:11:48.470 --> 00:11:50.303
He might've saw one of the segments.

00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:57.990
But he asked me some questions
and he came by the job site

00:11:57.990 --> 00:12:00.887
and he said, "Hey, you
know there's some things

00:12:00.887 --> 00:12:01.720
"you didn't know about me,

00:12:01.720 --> 00:12:04.360
"but my hobbies are this and this."

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:09.030
And I looked, I said,
"Okay, I had no idea."

00:12:09.030 --> 00:12:11.700
I'm like, "Man, I appreciate
you sharing that with me."

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:12.933
So that let me know.

00:12:14.655 --> 00:12:15.488
That let me know something

00:12:15.488 --> 00:12:17.110
that he's putting forth an effort.

00:12:18.570 --> 00:12:21.293
I'm not looking for no,

00:12:25.524 --> 00:12:26.865
(sighs)

00:12:26.865 --> 00:12:28.290
(stammers)

00:12:28.290 --> 00:12:31.630
I'm not looking for no apologies.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:33.480
Nothing like that from the past, man.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:35.860
It is what the fuck it is, man.

00:12:35.860 --> 00:12:37.363
We've had our experiences

00:12:37.363 --> 00:12:38.720
as growing up.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:39.840
We never been close,

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:41.030
we never had no relationship,

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:42.693
we've never had no close bond.

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.937
I told him, man, I said, "You know what?

00:12:46.937 --> 00:12:49.117
"You're a stranger to me.

00:12:49.117 --> 00:12:52.200
"You're a brother just
in wording, in saying."

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:54.577
I said, "I don't know
anything pertinent about you.

00:12:54.577 --> 00:12:55.980
"I don't know nothing important about you.

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.807
"I don't know your favorite color.

00:12:57.807 --> 00:12:59.507
"I don't know your favorite foods.

00:13:00.447 --> 00:13:01.617
"I don't know your hobbies.

00:13:01.617 --> 00:13:03.280
"None of that."

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:04.113
You know?

00:13:04.113 --> 00:13:06.797
I said, "We never did one
thing together growing up.

00:13:06.797 --> 00:13:08.537
"We never went to the
football game together.

00:13:08.537 --> 00:13:10.337
"We never played ball together.

00:13:10.337 --> 00:13:13.440
"We never went to the
movies together, nothing."

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.453
One-on-one.

00:13:16.050 --> 00:13:17.977
I said, "We have to
start off as strangers,

00:13:17.977 --> 00:13:19.367
"work at being friends,

00:13:19.367 --> 00:13:21.807
"and maybe one day we
can become brothers."

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:25.733
Because if we don't
start a strangers, man,

00:13:27.170 --> 00:13:29.300
then there will always
be a misunderstanding.

00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:30.863
There'll always be confusion.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:35.110
It'd be like it was,
man, back in the days,

00:13:35.110 --> 00:13:38.860
always bumping heads because
you're talking about,

00:13:38.860 --> 00:13:41.131
oh you my little brother and all that,

00:13:41.131 --> 00:13:43.460
you're my big brother,

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.270
but in actuality, man,

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:48.550
I've been gone 20-something
years off and on since the '80s.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:52.090
All of them 20-some
trips, 19 trips to prison,

00:13:52.090 --> 00:13:54.810
this two years, three
years, four years, nine,

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:56.540
when they do all that bullshit,

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.120
there's a lot we missed out on.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.630
So me coming out in 2017,

00:14:02.283 --> 00:14:03.853
I've been gone since 2011,

00:14:04.821 --> 00:14:06.380
you want to pick up
right where we left off.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.213
Shit.

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:11.190
Man, we got to start
from when we was kids.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.640
'Cause there's a lot missing right there.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:15.793
It ain't gray, it ain't no gray area.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:19.200
Shit, it's a black area.

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.220
It's black and white.

00:14:20.220 --> 00:14:21.230
Ain't no gray in between.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:24.440
It's black, white, and then a gray.

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.190
Black is just total absence.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.580
No communication, no nothing

00:14:30.580 --> 00:14:32.870
from different points of time.

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.283
Different periods of time.

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:39.970
So every time I'm around
him, I feel like a stranger.

00:14:39.970 --> 00:14:42.300
The only one I'm close to is my mother.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:43.210
Why?

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:45.300
Because she wrote me all the trips,

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:47.100
all the 19 trips to prison.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.380
She wrote me and stayed
in contact with me.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.710
That's how I was able to build
that relationship with her.

00:14:51.710 --> 00:14:53.330
It stayed like that with her,

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:55.323
those 19 motherfucking trips.

00:14:56.810 --> 00:14:58.820
But she filled me in on how my family,

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:00.570
my siblings was doing.

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:02.980
Oh Tracy's doing this, Todd's doing this,

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.943
Chris is doing that, Isaiah.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:09.710
So I'm looking at them through her eyes,

00:15:09.710 --> 00:15:10.860
through her experience,

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:13.440
but I have to have my
own experience with them

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:14.993
to get the full picture.

00:15:17.093 --> 00:15:18.550
I can't walk in nobody else's shoes

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.120
or nobody else's experience.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.433
It can guide me.

00:15:22.448 --> 00:15:24.020
I've got to walk with my own shoes,

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.400
have my own experiences

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:28.183
with Isaiah, Christopher, Todd, Tracy.

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:32.760
I've been home what? (stammers)

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.250
Three years.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.556
And I'm no closer to
building a relationship

00:15:36.556 --> 00:15:38.733
with none of them except my mama.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:41.230
I'm working on it

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.017
but I'm a work in progress, man.

00:15:43.017 --> 00:15:44.120
And the cool thing about it is

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:45.580
everybody have a
motherfucking life to live,

00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:47.260
everybody's doing their thing.

00:15:47.260 --> 00:15:50.200
And everybody's dealing with something.

00:15:50.200 --> 00:15:51.630
But everybody's above water,

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:52.913
so I'm cool with that.

00:15:54.280 --> 00:15:55.880
I'm cool with that.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.350
It's gonna take some time.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:59.990
Time might not be on my
side, it might, I don't know.

00:15:59.990 --> 00:16:01.130
Shit.

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:02.430
I'm not no fortune teller.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:07.643
But family,

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.610
it's a mystery.

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:12.773
Job, I'm learning.

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:17.220
But one thing about
work is I like working.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:19.160
I like hard work, you know?

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.630
Shit.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:23.823
Saturdays and Sunday, I do concrete.

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:28.520
I cement this woman's yard.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:32.163
She wants to make it into a parking lot,

00:16:32.163 --> 00:16:33.450
excuse me, a parking area,

00:16:33.450 --> 00:16:35.870
so her kids, her two sons
can park their vehicles

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.130
on the property instead of on the streets

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.810
'cause it get kind of crowded.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:43.810
And, man, doing an eight-hour day,

00:16:43.864 --> 00:16:48.864
I might lift about 75, 80,
60-pound bags of cement,

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:52.640
take them to a designated
area where the mixer is,

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:54.813
open them up and pour them into the mixer.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.220
Man, by the time I'm finished,

00:16:58.220 --> 00:17:01.400
it feels like I had worked out
in the gym like three hours.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:02.453
So in essence,

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:07.171
seven days a week, six
days a week, (stammers)

00:17:07.171 --> 00:17:08.550
I'm in the gym.

00:17:08.550 --> 00:17:10.100
But it's a different workout,

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:11.320
it's a different way.

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:14.237
And I feel it in different areas.

00:17:14.237 --> 00:17:16.970
I don't feel it in my chest,
my arms, my shoulders,

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.270
my back, my legs,

00:17:18.270 --> 00:17:21.730
but I do, but just it's
a different feeling.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:23.970
And most importantly,

00:17:23.970 --> 00:17:25.930
this kind of workout,

00:17:25.930 --> 00:17:27.450
it helps me from the inside out.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.650
It starts in my inner,

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:31.783
that self-esteem, that self-worth.

00:17:33.418 --> 00:17:38.063
It gives me, it builds character, shit.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:44.160
And what I'm being taught,
nobody can take away from me.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:46.250
And everything I'm being
taught is the right way

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.980
how to do some shit.

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.830
I know the right way how to lay cement.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.940
I know the right way how to paint.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.890
I know the right way how to do a floor.

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:59.760
So my teachers, the men
that are in my life,

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:02.240
the three men that I'm dealing with,

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.370
they're giving me the right information,

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:08.270
the right tools to succeed
in these three areas,

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.970
which enables me to succeed in life.

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:12.790
Now I have to work on
dealing with my family

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:15.071
in that area because
it hasn't transformed.

00:18:15.071 --> 00:18:19.043
It haven't manifested in that area yet.

00:18:20.300 --> 00:18:23.070
But if I can just stay on
the straight and narrow

00:18:23.070 --> 00:18:25.850
and get these experiences
from these different jobs

00:18:25.850 --> 00:18:28.980
that I'm doing and learn them,

00:18:28.980 --> 00:18:32.173
then it'll roll over into different areas.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:36.880
I think (sighs)

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.090
it took me three days

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:41.800
to learn how to paint real good.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:42.750
I mean, for real, for real.

00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:43.893
It took me three days.

00:18:44.728 --> 00:18:47.050
It took me about two
weeks how to do the cement

00:18:49.135 --> 00:18:52.253
and about one week how to
work how to work the floor.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:57.220
And I wish it was like
that with my family.

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:01.240
I wish it was like that with life.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.100
But it's not, man, it's not.

00:19:03.100 --> 00:19:04.850
I still have two left feet.

00:19:04.850 --> 00:19:06.520
It's easy for my ass to trip.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:09.350
I have to be careful, always.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:11.470
There's not a day that I can let up.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:13.990
There's not a day, man,

00:19:13.990 --> 00:19:14.840
that I can just

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:20.337
wake up in the morning
and think to myself,

00:19:20.337 --> 00:19:21.997
"Oh, today I'm just going to bullshit,

00:19:21.997 --> 00:19:24.070
"lay around and do nothing."

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:27.060
I'm not gonna pray, I'm not
gonna meditate, (stammers)

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.063
I'm gonna just say F it, you know?

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.870
And when I think about those days,

00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.170
I'll know right where I ended up,

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.730
in prison, in a crack house on the side

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:41.008
of the motherfucking freeway off ramp.

00:19:41.008 --> 00:19:41.950
And I don't want that today.

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.550
I want something more than that.

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:45.650
I deserve more than that.

00:19:45.650 --> 00:19:47.050
I owe myself more than that.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.183
Shit, life is scary.

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:53.490
'Cause I've escaped.

00:19:53.490 --> 00:19:56.780
I've been running for so
long, ran over 30 years.

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:59.160
And all of a sudden, I
got almost three years

00:19:59.160 --> 00:20:00.700
of dealing with some shit.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.360
And at the time, I didn't
want to deal with it.

00:20:03.360 --> 00:20:06.810
Up until they shut down the gyms.

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:08.500
Then my foundation was crushed

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:11.220
because that was my
foundation, the gym, my body,

00:20:11.220 --> 00:20:12.213
how I looked.

00:20:14.078 --> 00:20:15.076
That's all I had.

00:20:15.076 --> 00:20:17.983
That's all I had to offer
to the world as I know it.

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:23.760
But lo and behold, there was
more to me than I even knew.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:24.860
I didn't believe enough.

00:20:24.860 --> 00:20:27.470
I couldn't even see it what I see now.

00:20:27.470 --> 00:20:29.590
But the cool thing about it is
instead of seeing some shit,

00:20:29.590 --> 00:20:30.423
I'm living some shit.

00:20:30.423 --> 00:20:31.590
That's the difference.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:32.790
I'm living it.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.393
Living my motherfucking dream.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.243
What's that?

00:20:36.243 --> 00:20:38.310
Doing the things I never thought I'd do.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.690
Doing shit I was supposed
to do my 20s, 30s, and 40s.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:41.840
Doing that shit in 50s.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:48.843
That's one of those unspoken
prayers that's being answered.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:52.333
Shit.

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:56.503
It ain't easy.

00:20:59.275 --> 00:21:00.525
But it's okay, it's okay.

00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:06.733
Never thought I'd be here.

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:09.880
Never thought I'd be in
his position, this place,

00:21:09.880 --> 00:21:11.780
mind, body, and spirit.

00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:13.150
When I wake up in the morning

00:21:13.150 --> 00:21:17.003
and the first thing I think
about is being on time.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.490
How hard I'm gonna do today.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:24.563
What I'm gonna do.

00:21:25.913 --> 00:21:29.560
And when I get there, put
forth the effort, man.

00:21:29.560 --> 00:21:32.180
Do the best that I can do
throughout the day, man.

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:33.550
And that's it.

00:21:33.550 --> 00:21:35.020
And when I'm coming back,

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.550
you know the cool thing
about it is when I leave,

00:21:37.550 --> 00:21:40.220
instead of getting picked up by my boss,

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:42.610
I catch the bus and train to the job site

00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:46.420
just so I have time just to
relax and get my mind together,

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:49.670
to deal with whatever day has in store.

00:21:49.670 --> 00:21:51.550
It's the same when I
get finished with work.

00:21:51.550 --> 00:21:53.900
I have my boss take me
to the train station

00:21:53.900 --> 00:21:56.458
or the bus station, (stammers)

00:21:56.458 --> 00:21:59.520
so I have time just to unwind
from what I experienced

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:04.090
and just let it, let
it marinate, you know?

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:07.750
And by the time I get home, I'm good.

00:22:07.750 --> 00:22:08.833
I'm with me.

00:22:09.865 --> 00:22:10.929
With me.

00:22:10.929 --> 00:22:11.762
With me.

00:22:12.707 --> 00:22:13.540
It ain't about them,

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:15.410
it ain't about the double-takes
when motherfuckers look,

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:17.140
it ain't about that no more.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:19.200
I don't even trip on that.

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:20.033
I'm not even,

00:22:20.033 --> 00:22:23.400
I haven't been in a relationship
in about nine months.

00:22:23.400 --> 00:22:25.330
I'm not on the bus and
trains looking at people

00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:27.000
and trying to get at the women.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:27.850
I admire them.

00:22:27.850 --> 00:22:28.683
I love them.

00:22:28.683 --> 00:22:29.850
I love them all.

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:31.290
I love women.

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:33.720
Shit, I ain't tripping on that.

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:34.553
But the point is,

00:22:34.553 --> 00:22:35.386
I'm not out there

00:22:35.386 --> 00:22:38.000
trying to get in no relationship
or nothing like that, man.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:39.860
I'm just out and dealing with life,

00:22:39.860 --> 00:22:41.523
enjoying it for what it is, man.

00:22:42.890 --> 00:22:46.400
And when it's the right time,

00:22:46.400 --> 00:22:47.840
God's gonna put her in my life.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:49.800
I'm not worried about that.

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:51.680
But my thing is everything
that I thought would

00:22:51.680 --> 00:22:55.820
make me happy, it was
all from the outside.

00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:59.533
But what really makes me
happy is having the courage

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:05.963
to get up and face another
day, come what may.

00:23:09.950 --> 00:23:11.030
That's it, man.

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:11.873
In a nutshell.

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:14.200
There's so much I want,

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.910
but what I really need is to keep doing

00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:17.900
what the fuck I'm doing,

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:20.163
staying in my lane and out the way.

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:24.543
Shit.

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:27.080
I want everything.

00:23:27.080 --> 00:23:28.073
I want it all.

00:23:31.462 --> 00:23:33.023
But I'm gonna get me what
I need just to make it

00:23:33.023 --> 00:23:34.263
through the day.

00:23:37.037 --> 00:23:38.537
And that's enough for me, man.

00:23:39.891 --> 00:23:40.724
That's enough for me.

00:23:40.724 --> 00:23:42.840
There's so much more that I can talk about

00:23:42.840 --> 00:23:47.840
when it comes to being home, being free,

00:23:48.040 --> 00:23:51.780
and trying to navigate life on like terms,

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.430
not on my terms.

00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.490
If it was on my terms, I have a car,

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:59.500
I have a two-bedroom apartment,
I'd be in a relationship,

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:03.453
have kids, a motorboat, mobile home.

00:24:04.330 --> 00:24:06.780
I have the merry-go-round
in the back of the yard

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:10.563
and all that bullshit,
10 kids running around.

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:16.823
But in reality, all I got is me.

00:24:19.169 --> 00:24:21.513
And I have to depend on me, love on me,

00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:24.170
and treat me and all that bullshit, man.

00:24:24.170 --> 00:24:25.383
And sometimes it,

00:24:25.383 --> 00:24:26.991
(stammers)

00:24:26.991 --> 00:24:28.280
(sighs)

00:24:28.280 --> 00:24:30.363
it's scary, to be honest with you.

00:24:31.843 --> 00:24:33.340
(stammers)

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:36.300
'Cause I'm by myself, I'm
alone, and I have to do this.

00:24:36.300 --> 00:24:37.627
I have some assistance.

00:24:37.627 --> 00:24:40.270
I get suggestions and stuff like that.

00:24:40.270 --> 00:24:42.350
But when it's all said and done,

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:44.450
I have to put one foot in front
of the motherfucking other.

00:24:44.450 --> 00:24:46.780
I don't give a fuck if
somebody take me by the hand

00:24:46.780 --> 00:24:48.163
and just guide me.

00:24:49.100 --> 00:24:50.290
I still got to do it.

00:24:50.290 --> 00:24:54.560
I still got to do my part
and that's what's scary.

00:24:58.640 --> 00:25:00.590
It's scary but at the same time,

00:25:00.590 --> 00:25:03.490
it gives me the freedom to go
where I've never gone before,

00:25:03.490 --> 00:25:05.340
to be who I never thought I'd become.

00:25:07.360 --> 00:25:09.313
I wouldn't trade it for nothing else.

00:25:10.550 --> 00:25:14.140
And like I said,

00:25:14.140 --> 00:25:15.700
there's so much more
I can talk about, man,

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:18.163
but the bottom line is,

00:25:21.487 --> 00:25:22.449
(sighs)

00:25:22.449 --> 00:25:25.560
I only get one chance at this.

00:25:25.560 --> 00:25:26.393
And,

00:25:28.169 --> 00:25:30.990
(sighs)

00:25:30.990 --> 00:25:34.073
it's about time that I showed up.

00:25:35.640 --> 00:25:39.070
And I'm just glad, man,

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:40.660
that I have the opportunity

00:25:40.660 --> 00:25:43.173
to put my money where my mouth is.

00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:47.830
So today I let my actions
speak louder than my words.

00:25:47.830 --> 00:25:49.940
I talk a good one but I
can show you some shit

00:25:49.940 --> 00:25:53.600
I learned today and my work is good.

00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:54.550
Yeah.

00:25:54.550 --> 00:25:55.630
Bet your last dollar.

00:25:55.630 --> 00:25:57.110
You can take that
motherfucking check to the bank

00:25:57.110 --> 00:25:57.943
and cash it.

00:25:58.847 --> 00:26:00.497
I've got something to offer today

00:26:01.460 --> 00:26:04.280
and it ain't my body, it ain't my looks.

00:26:04.280 --> 00:26:06.970
I've got some real
skills to pay the bills.

00:26:06.970 --> 00:26:08.050
Holler.

00:26:08.050 --> 00:26:08.883
Thank you.

